Subject: [PATCH 0/3] powerpc: exit-path return values under CONFIG_GENERIC_ENTRY
To: Madhavan Srinivasan <maddy@linux.ibm.com>
Cc: Michael Ellerman <mpe@ellerman.id.au>,
    Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>,
    Christophe Leroy <chleroy@kernel.org>,
    linuxppc-dev@lists.ozlabs.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

Three related fixes in the powerpc entry/exit path, all reachable since
powerpc selected CONFIG_GENERIC_ENTRY in 7.2.

Patches 1 and 3 concern the value the exit assembly in interrupt_64.S uses
to decide between restoring the full register set from pt_regs and the fast
path that does not. In both cases an accumulated _TIF_RESTOREALL is
discarded before the assembly can test it -- patch 1 by returning the
per-restart value instead of the accumulated one, patch 3 by clearing
exit_flags after the exit work that sets it has already run rather than
before.

Patch 2 is independent and user-visible. When seccomp or ptrace skips a
syscall, powerpc returns -ENOSYS instead of the value the tracer already
stored in pt_regs, so every SECCOMP_RET_ERRNO(x) arrives in userspace as
ENOSYS. It was found from a sandboxed Chromium reporting ENOSYS for
broker-denied opens.

  1/3  powerpc/64: return the accumulated exit_result from syscall_exit_restart()
  2/3  powerpc/syscall: keep the seccomp/ptrace return value when the syscall is skipped
  3/3  powerpc: clear exit_flags before the interrupt exit work runs

Testing
-------
All three have been built into 7.2.6 and are running as the daily driver on
an IBM AC922 (2x POWER9, 176 threads, 64K pages) since 2026-09-16, through
full desktop and heavy package-build workloads.

Patch 2 additionally has a standalone reproducer: a SECCOMP_RET_ERRNO
filter checked over five errno values through both glibc's scv 0 path and
raw sc. Every case delivers the filter's errno with the patch applied and
ENOSYS without it. I am happy to send it as a seccomp selftest if that is
the preferred form.

Caveats
-------
No Fixes: tags. These were developed against a release tarball rather than
a git tree, so I have not identified the introducing commits; I expect all
three date from the generic-entry conversion. Happy to add the tags if
someone can point me at the right commits, or to respin against mainline --
the series is on 7.2.6 and applies cleanly there.

I am not a powerpc maintainer and would welcome correction on patches 1 and
3 in particular: the mechanism is clear from the code, but I have not
constructed a targeted reproducer for either, so the evidence for them is
"the machine runs correctly with them applied" rather than a demonstrated
failure without.

Jordan Bettcher (3):
  powerpc/64: return the accumulated exit_result from
    syscall_exit_restart()
  powerpc/syscall: keep the seccomp/ptrace return value when the syscall
